{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/977540-outside-of-emergencies-and-utility-why-would-you-ever-show-your-demonic-form","id":977540,"title":"Outside of emergencies and utility why would you ever show your demonic form?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T19:44:57-07:00","id":977540,"title":"Outside of emergencies and utility why would you ever show your demonic form?","content":"One thing I don't like about demon, is you spend all this time creating a demonic form, that you're then heavily penalized for unveiling. Obviously demons wouldn't think it's cool, it's their bodies after all (though there are people like that...). Outside of some extreme cases, like going loud, or to utilize a piece of your form it seems discouraged. There don't even appear to be good social reasons for showing it. Am I missing something? Has anyone ever tried making a system where constant use of covers cost maintenance? or provided some other encouragement to look like a devil? This is especially important to me as a GM, because... why would my NPCs ever look like Demons (I see in the STG there are some, but I haven't been able to figure out why they would retain that form).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T19:55:03-07:00","id":977546,"title":"","content":"For one thing, they're more comfortable in their demonic forms. You don't want to wear your meat suit if you don't have to. Then there's the full Aether refresh as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:02:54-07:00","id":977554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/977540-outside-of-emergencies-and-utility-why-would-you-ever-show-your-demonic-form?p=977546#post977546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, they're more comfortable in their demonic forms. You don't want to wear your meat suit if you don't have to. Then there's the full Aether refresh as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full Aether refresh (page?)? also how have I missed this comfort thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:20:55-07:00","id":977562,"title":"","content":"It doesn't approach full until higher levels of Primum (going loud, however, is always a full refill), but corebook p. 195:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The demon heals lethal or bashing damage equal to her Primum rating, starting with the rightmost health box upon changing into her demonic form. Any Tilts relating to a bodily injury, such as Arm Wrack, are removed.<br /> When the demon shifts into her demonic form, she is more attuned to the Aether around her. She can draw in the little bits of processes and mechanisms floating about within the air to fuel her without much conscious effort. The Unchained gains a number of Aether equal to her Primum on her initial transformation into demonic form. Because she is so attuned to the Aether, she can never truly run out of it. Whenever her Aether is reduced to zero, the player can roll Primum, and each success gains the demon one Aether (minimum 1, even if the roll fails). </div> </div> </div>So as your Primum increases (and Cipher progression means demons rise to mid-level Primum faster than other supernatural types), it gets to be pretty good healing and Aether restock. Not the best option in either case, but a nice bonus on top of gaining the use of your form abilities.<br /> <br /> What use demons have for their demonic form depends on their form ability loadout. A demon with a Rivet Arm, a Plasma Drive, and an Eliminator Cannon is going to end up saving his revelation for violent emergencies and dramatic shock assaults, whereas one with Mirrored Skin, Wings, and Insect Swarm is going to have a lot more nonviolent occasions to get a lot of use out of their quantum form. But really, just looking at the thread title, &quot;outside of emergencies and utility, why would you show your demonic form?&quot; You mostly wouldn't, except maybe on dramatic moments or for specific character reasons. But you're playing a spy thriller. Emergency situations and opportunities for useful risk-taking are going to be in plentiful supply. Players like to get up to extreme situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:40:23-07:00","id":977574,"title":"","content":"Wow, I remembered that <i>completely</i> wrong. That's the bit I was referring to, though.<br /> <br /> The comfort thing is on page 43<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some demons feel much more comfortable in their demonic form, to the point that they try to arrange their lives so that they can spend some time that way every day. These demons sometimes band together to create safe spaces where they can assume their demonic forms and \u201clet their hair down\u201d without worrying about curious humans or the God-Machine\u2019s agents. Where they exist, these places are often neutral ground where Demons with radically different outlooks \u2014 Saboteurs and Integrators, the most radically pro-human demons and the most selfish and abusive Tempters \u2014 can meet. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-27-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T21:11:07-07:00","id":977586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming demonic form: Fully shedding human form and<br /> taking demonic shape is always a compromise. This roll is<br /> made at a \u20133 penalty. Staying in demonic form for longer<br /> than a scene is likewise a compromise, with a further \u20131<br /> penalty per scene (see Full Transformation, p. 195). </div> </div> </div>do you guys play it out like this if no one is around to see it? and what about those places demons go... where there are only demons... or boltholes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T12:23:30-07:00","id":977891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/977540-outside-of-emergencies-and-utility-why-would-you-ever-show-your-demonic-form?p=977586#post977586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> do you guys play it out like this if no one is around to see it? and what about those places demons go... where there are only demons... or boltholes...</div> </div> </div> </div>I do yeah, it is one of the big driving forces for many Demons search for Hell. To find a place where they can be in Demonic form without worrying about the God Machine.<br /> <br /> I did have a night club inspired by Papa Midnight's in Constantine. Where an Interlock based on the Embed Interference is used to make it safe(ish) to be in demonic form. It requires a ton of effort and there is still a risk of it failing and being raided (plot hooks ^_^).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:05:39-07:00","id":978335,"title":"","content":"Outside of utility? There's a hell of a lot of utility in demon forms. You're faster, stronger, smarter, prettier, and just... more. There is the aether thing. Honestly, I find it difficult that most demons won't want to flash their true forms every once in a while because of the sheer amount of benefits in lots of areas. <br /> <br /> As for the rooms where demons &quot;let their hair down,&quot; there's the aether/compromise dampening wood mentioned in the core book. Bolt holes and modified suborned infrastructure are a thing. In my game, I had gadgets built with the Interference Embed and the Context Matters Exploit around the area - this effectively reduced the chances of a compromise to something negligable. Its like Elysium in VtR - you have a decreased chance of frenzy there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:05:18-07:00","id":978780,"title":"","content":"In my games... well, basically never.<br /> <br /> Really, in my games it seems to be reserved for demon-fighting and other emergencies. Better risking cover than being gunned down by four thugs, for example. Or risking cover to face another demon (demon vs demon is a big thing in my game) rather than being eviscerated.<br /> <br /> I think they think about it like Spawn's limited power supply: It's very powerful, but can't be used unless the penalties for <i>not</i> using it outweight the penalties for actually using your form.<br /> <br /> They seem to be pretty liberal with partial transformation however, specially single-ability ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11854-dibastet","name":"DiBastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T17:51:33-07:00","id":1396086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/977540-outside-of-emergencies-and-utility-why-would-you-ever-show-your-demonic-form?p=977574#post977574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, I remembered that <i>completely</i> wrong. That's the bit I was referring to, though.<br /> <br /> The comfort thing is on page 43</div> </div> </div> </div>...... Just came up with a Plot Hook. Thanks for the Inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}